# Lab 20: Agent Registration collection probe
#
# Purpose:
# Test whether the tenant exposes an undocumented read-only collection endpoint
# for agent registrations.
#
# Current first-party documentation only describes:
#   GET /beta/copilot/agentRegistrations/{id}
#
# It does not describe:
#   GET /beta/copilot/agentRegistrations
#
# This is therefore a bounded negative probe, not use of a supported list API.
# Do not build implementation logic on a 200 response without first-party
# documentation confirming that the collection endpoint is supported.
#
# Required delegated permission:
#   AgentRegistration.Read.All
#
# Keep tenant ID and client ID in the ignored .env used by index.http.

@tenantId = {{$dotenv A365_TENANT_ID}}
@clientId = {{$dotenv A365_CLIENT_ID}}
@graphBaseUrl = https://graph.microsoft.com
@registrationReadScope = https%3A%2F%2Fgraph.microsoft.com%2FAgentRegistration.Read.All%20offline_access

###############################################################################
# Step R1 - Start device-code authentication
#
# Expected:
#   200 OK with user_code, device_code, and verification_uri.
#
# A 400 response mentioning invalid_scope or consent means the app is not
# configured or consented for AgentRegistration.Read.All.

# @name registrationDeviceCode
POST https://login.microsoftonline.com/{{tenantId}}/oauth2/v2.0/devicecode
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

client_id={{clientId}}&scope={{registrationReadScope}}

###

###############################################################################
# Step R2 - Complete sign-in
#
# Open verification_uri from R1, enter user_code, and sign in locally.
# Do not share either code.

###############################################################################
# Step R3 - Exchange the device code for a token
#
# Expected:
#   200 OK with scope containing AgentRegistration.Read.All.
#
# authorization_pending means R2 has not completed. Retry after the interval
# returned by R1. Never save or share this response.

# @name registrationToken
POST https://login.microsoftonline.com/{{tenantId}}/oauth2/v2.0/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=urn%3Aietf%3Aparams%3Aoauth%3Agrant-type%3Adevice_code&client_id={{clientId}}&device_code={{registrationDeviceCode.response.body.$.device_code}}

###

###############################################################################
# Step R4 - Probe the undocumented registration collection endpoint
#
# URL:
#   GET https://graph.microsoft.com/beta/copilot/agentRegistrations
#
# Interpret only the status and response shape:
#
# 200 OK
#   The endpoint currently responds with a collection in this tenant.
#   This is observable behavior, but remains undocumented and unsuitable for
#   committed implementation until Microsoft documents support.
#
# 400 Bad Request, 404 Not Found, or 405 Method Not Allowed
#   No usable collection endpoint was observed.
#
# 401 Unauthorized
#   Authentication failed; the endpoint capability was not tested.
#
# 403 Forbidden
#   Permission or role denied the request; the endpoint capability remains
#   inconclusive.
#
# Do not save or share a successful response body because it can contain all
# tenant registration identifiers and metadata.

# @name listAgentRegistrationsProbe
GET {{graphBaseUrl}}/beta/copilot/agentRegistrations
Authorization: Bearer {{registrationToken.response.body.$.access_token}}
Accept: application/json

###

###############################################################################
# Stop after R4
#
# Do not POST, PATCH, or DELETE any registration in this probe.
